`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`
The generation-counter pattern (`refreshGen`) here is the standard fix for the classic "stale timer" race in Bubble Tea's Elm-architecture model: because `tea.Cmd`s are just functions returning a message at some future point, you can't cancel an already-scheduled `refreshTickCmd`. Instead, each scheduled tick carries the generation it belongs to; `Update` compares that against the model's *current* generation and silently drops the message if they don't match. Bumping the counter on manual refresh is cheaper than plumbing real cancellation through `tea.Cmd`, and it composes for free with the fetch-in-flight skip (a second orthogonal check on `isRefreshing`).
`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`

